WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:04.842
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> ‘Welcome to Denver Airport. How can I help you today?’

2
00:00:05.226 --> 00:00:12.087
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> I handed my passport and flight confirmation to the woman at United Airlines check-in.

3
00:00:12.271 --> 00:00:19.801
I was on my way to Costa Rica at the beginning of the trip of a lifetime, travelling around Central America.

4
00:00:20.218 --> 00:00:24.726
The woman checked in my backpack and handed me my boarding pass.

5
00:00:24.926 --> 00:00:29.133
‘Lucky you, going to California,’ she smiled.

6
00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:31.738
‘Your gate is 37C.’

7
00:00:32.105 --> 00:00:36.012
‘No. I booked a ticket to San José.’

8
00:00:36.229 --> 00:00:41.154
‘Yes, dear. Your ticket is for San José, in California.’

9
00:00:41.387 --> 00:00:44.526
I was horrified!

10
00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:51.638
‘I’m so sorry, but I need your help. My ticket is for the wrong San José.’

11
00:00:52.189 --> 00:00:58.517
This time she didn’t smile. She pointed to the help desk for United Airlines.

12
00:00:58.867 --> 00:01:05.195
The next few hours were terrible. The help desk assistant wasn’t helpful.

13
00:01:05.529 --> 00:01:08.734
‘I’m sorry. We can’t change your ticket.’

14
00:01:09.185 --> 00:01:15.062
I tried to call my travel agent, hoping they could solve the problem. No luck.

15
00:01:15.579 --> 00:01:18.718
A message arrived on my phone from my dad.

16
00:01:18.818 --> 00:01:25.830
It was a link to the Dionne Warwick song ‘Do you know the way to San José?’ Not funny, Dad.

17
00:01:26.047 --> 00:01:34.061
Then a new assistant arrived. ‘What’s the problem?’ she asked. I explained the situation.

18
00:01:34.328 --> 00:01:39.220
‘Of course we can book a new flight for you, dear.’ I hugged her.

19
00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:44.913
She immediately booked me onto a cheap flight to San José, Costa Rica.

20
00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:50.823
Suddenly, I remembered my backpack. But it was too late.

21
00:01:51.173 --> 00:01:54.479
‘Did you check in my luggage?’ I asked.

22
00:01:54.646 --> 00:01:59.204
‘No. Unfortunately, it’s on the way to California.’

23
00:01:59.538 --> 00:02:10.640
So, after 72 hours, four flights, and three days without luggage, I can say that I know the (long) way to San José.

24
00:02:10.857 --> 00:02:19.488
And I have one important lesson for you: always take spare underwear in your carry-on luggage.

25
00:02:19.722 --> 00:02:26.283
And if you can fit extra jeans, a T-shirt and a sweater in there too, DO THAT!